mathdb-lean problems
====================

This repository publishes benchmark releases of mathematical problems formalized
in Lean 4, together with the pinned Lean project they compile against.

VENDORED LIBRARIES
------------------

`project/lean/` carries two Lean libraries taken from Formal Conjectures
(https://github.com/google-deepmind/formal-conjectures), which is licensed under
the Apache License, Version 2.0:

  upstream FormalConjecturesUtil/         -> MathdbUtil/,     MathdbUtil.lean
  upstream FormalConjecturesForMathlib/   -> MathdbMathlib/,  MathdbMathlib.lean
  LICENSE  lean-toolchain  lake-manifest.json  (unchanged)

CHANGES FROM UPSTREAM, as Apache 2.0 section 4(b) requires them to be stated:
the two libraries' *module* names were changed to the two shown above, and their
`import` lines and `lakefile.toml` entries were rewritten to match. Nothing else
was touched. In particular every Lean *namespace* inside them is upstream's,
including `Google`, which holds the `answer()` elaborator, `FormalConjectures
.Metadata`, and one per linter. No declaration, statement, proof or docstring was
added, removed or edited.

The upstream revision is recorded in each problem's `problem.toml` as
`[source] revision`, and in `benchmark.json`.

PROBLEM STATEMENTS
------------------

The problem modules under `problems/` are derived mechanically from that same
upstream revision's `FormalConjectures/ErdosProblems/*.lean`, which is likewise
Apache-2.0. Each module records the upstream file, theorem name and revision it
came from in its own metadata block, and each `problem.toml` records the same.
They are generated by the mathdb-lean problem library, which is maintained
separately; this repository holds its output.

Formal Conjectures is a project of Google DeepMind and the Formal Conjectures
Authors, listed below. This repository is not affiliated with or endorsed by
them.

